</span><div class="gd-t">Post it. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> on Today and paste the listing&#39;s address. Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> the same way when you do those.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and &quot;send your number&quot;, filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car&#39;s link or asks for a phone number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">After answering the inbox, open <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today&#39;s. A price change marks the live listing <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and opens the usual update task.</li><li>A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says <b class="gd-ui">Do not post yet</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rotation settings</b> change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car&#39;s home area wins).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The team&#39;s listings</b>: Sales post from their own profiles under <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b>, each listing in its own copy variant (title, description, photo order and cover), so no ad is posted twice. A car has at most 5 live listings, yours included (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Facebook Marketplace</b>). The card lists who posted what, its status, when it ends and the listing&#39;s address. Your own posts and renewals still count against your o