Cal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-out: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. The search above it finds any booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'marketing-on-facebook-marketplace', 'chapter', 'sales', null, 'Marketing on Facebook Marketplace', 'Your own listings from your own profile, never the same ad twice, the auto-reply, the inbox and your Claude.',
  '**Sales** > **Marketing**. You post CarmaCars cars on Facebook Marketplace from your own Facebook profile, answer the Marketplace inbox, and log what you did. The numbers you collect are leads credited to you.

## Never the same ad twice

Each car can have up to 5 live listings across the team (the owner''s own listing included). Every listing is a different **copy variant**: its own title, its own description wording, its own photo order and its own cover photo. When you claim a car, its variant is yours until you take the listing down or it lapses: no one else can post that copy. You can have one listing of a car at a time.

- A claim you do not post within a day lets go by itself.
- A listing ends 30 days after you posted or renewed it, unless you renew it.
- The Admin sees who posted what, with the listing''s address.

## Today

1. **Today** lists your work in this order: **Take down**, **Update the price**, **Post it** (a car you claimed), then **Renew** and new **Post** items, up to your posts and renewals for the day (4 by default).
2. On a **Post** item press **Claim variant** with its number. Then press **Kit**.
3. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in order, each with **Copy**, your variant''s description and tracked link, and the photos in your order. Press **Download the photos (ZIP)**: 01 is your cover.
4. Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on **Today**, press **Posted** and paste the address. **Let go** frees a claim you will not post.
5. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** when you do those on Facebook.

## Words to use

Nothing a buyer reads says "rent", "rental" or "for rent". Every listing keeps the line "Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale" and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.

## The auto-reply

**Auto-reply for this listing** has the steps and the text, with your listing''s own link. While posting, scroll to **Auto replies** (or **Meta AI replies**), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first "Is this available?".

## The inbox

1. Open facebook.com/marketplace/inbox, the Selling tab, oldest first.
2. Use **Inbox replies for this car** only: price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery, send your number. One message per reply, at most two to someone who does not answer.
3. Then **Log an inbox session**: the chats, the replies and every number, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number is a lead credited to you, with a call-back task within 15 minutes.

## Your own Claude

**Your Claude in Chrome** has the instructions to paste into Claude in your own Chrome, and the **Academy lesson** that teaches them. Claude follows the same rules: the kit''s words and the templates only, it stops at any Facebook security check or CAPTCHA and tells you, it never types a password, and it logs every post in your Marketing tab.

> Watch out: Stop and tell the Admin if Facebook removes a listing or restricts your account. Do not appeal and do not post it again.',
  '<p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b>. You post CarmaCars cars on Facebook Marketplace from your own Facebook profile, answer the Marketplace inbox, and log what you did. The numbers you collect are leads credited to you.</p><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-never-the-same-ad-twice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Never the same ad twice</h2><p class="gd-p">Each car can have up to 5 live listings across the team (the owner&#39;s own listing included). Every listing is a different <b class="gd-ui">copy variant</b>: its own title, its own description wording, its own photo order and its own cover photo. When you claim a car, its variant is yours until you take the listing down or it lapses: no one else can post that copy. You can have one listing of a car at a time.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A claim you do not post within a day lets go by itself.</li><li>A listing ends 30 days after you posted or renewed it, unless you renew it.</li><li>The Admin sees who posted what, with the listing&#39;s address.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-today" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Today</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> lists your work in this order: <b class="gd-ui">Take down</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Post it</b> (a car you claimed), then <b class="gd-ui">Renew</b> and new <b class="gd-ui">Post</b> items, up to your posts and renewals for the day (4 by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a <b class="gd-ui">Post</b> item press <b class="gd-ui">Claim variant</b> with its number. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Kit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in order, each with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, your variant&#39;s description and tracked link, and the photos in your order. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the photos (ZIP)</b>: 01 is your cover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> and paste the address. <b class="gd-ui">Let go</b> frees a claim you will not post.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> when you do those on Facebook.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-words-to-use" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Words to use</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing a buyer reads says &quot;rent&quot;, &quot;rental&quot; or &quot;for rent&quot;. Every listing keeps the line &quot;Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale&quot; and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-auto-reply" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The auto-reply</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Auto-reply for this listing</b> has the steps and the text, with your listing&#39;s own link. While posting, scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Auto replies</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Meta AI replies</b>), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first &quot;Is this available?&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-inbox" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The inbox</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open facebook.com/marketplace/inbox, the Selling tab, oldest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Use <b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> only: price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery, send your number. One message per reply, at most two to someone who does not answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Then <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>: the chats, the replies and every number, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number is a lead credited to you, with a call-back task within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-your-own-claude" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your own Claude</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your Claude in Chrome</b> has the instructions to paste into Claude in your own Chrome, and the <b class="gd-ui">Academy lesson</b> that teaches them. Claude follows the same rules: the kit&#39;s words and the templates only, it stops at any Facebook security check or CAPTCHA and tells you, it never types a password, and it logs every post in your Marketing tab.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Stop and tell the Admin if Facebook removes a listing or restricts your account. Do not appeal and do not post it again.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'add-a-rental-by-hand', 'chapter', 'marketing-on-facebook-marketplace', 'Every function adds rentals that come in by phone, at the counter, from Turo, a partner, an insurer or someone you know. The rental is confirmed and on the calendar at once.

## Add a rental

Open **Bookings** > **Add a rental**. Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. At pickup with the renter? Press **Start at pickup**: the renter''s name and phone, the car, the kilometres and the fuel, then **Hold the car and finish later**. The car is held for 2 hours and you get a task to finish it.
2. Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (**Save draft** saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Today and on this page, opens a draft where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type.
3. Choose the car, the dates and the places. The check shows any clash with another booking or with the cleaning time after a trip. You cannot book over a clash: ask an Admin.
4. The dates decide the case, shown under them. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: the rental is recorded as on trip, and anything still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit) becomes a task. A rental that has already ended is recorded by an Admin.
5. Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one with their name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.
6. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves once the car and the dates are in. The price comes from the rate sheet. You may add the extras, how damage is covered and an allowed promo code.
7. Quick start: **Phone**, **Walk-in**, **Turo or another platform** or **Insurance replacement** sets the usual choices.
8. A car tagged Listing not finished can be rented too: it stays off the public site. If it has no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason. An owner''s car not yet on the fleet insurance policy is added by an Admin only.
9. Every line of the price can be changed where it stands (customer service and sales, while Program settings allow it): the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the kilometres a day; add a fee from the list or a charge of its own. The (i) beside each line says what it is. The rate-sheet price stays on the booking; a price far under it is flagged for an Admin, never refused. Know what the renter paid with tax? Choose After tax (HST included) under Amounts I type and type those amounts ("$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan"), or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that. The total shown is the total saved.
10. Any length: past 30 days the monthly rate applies for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. Each later period gets its own agreement, sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Monthly periods on the booking; Send the agreement for the next period now if needed).
11. Choose how the rent is paid (e-Transfer or cash received, card on file, payment link, platform payout, insurer billed later; the ways open to you are set by an Admin; paid in parts: Add another payment) and then how the deposit is paid (card hold, cash or e-Transfer with its reference). Before you save sums it all up. Signed on paper already? Choose it: a task asks for the scan. An insurance replacement with dates not known yet: untick Blocks the car''s calendar and say why. Insurer billed later shows Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver that the insurer authorized (empty: none); each is the rate times the days, plus HST, billed to the insurer.
12. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**.
13. Press **Add the rental**. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick **Do not email the renter**.
14. A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.

> Tip: The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal before pickup. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign. If they sign on paper at the counter, an Admin records it. A payment link keeps the booking waiting for payment.
', 'Add a rental by hand', 'Choose the car and dates, find the renter, price it, record how it is paid.',
