s open; otherwise it waits in the customer service queue. Call back with the Call button, or text, then mark the task done. Quo itself texts the caller back, so do not send the same message again.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A number that texted STOP gets no texts from us, booking texts included, until they text START. Prices go in a quote, never in a text from memory.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-email-text-or-both" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email, text or both</h2><p class="gd-p">Each renter and owner chooses how we reach them. Their page in Admin shows it under How we reach them; ask an Admin, or change it there if you can open the page. Texts need a phone they verified with a code. Your own choice is on your Profile, under Messages.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b> (customer service and Sales); press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin can switch the buttons back to the phone&#39;s own apps in Program settings. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'add-ons', 'chapter', 'discount-game-leads', 'Renters buy add-ons with a rental: seats, flowers, a chauffeur, an umbrella, a phone charger, a full tank. You add them in offers and rentals, confirm the ones that need it, and Fleet keeps the stock.

## In an offer or a rental you add

1. On the review screen of a request, under Add-ons, tick or count what the renter wants. The price on the right follows. Choose the hours for a chauffeur.
2. Add-ons the renter asked for are already ticked. One waiting for confirmation (a chauffeur) is confirmed when you keep it and send the offer; untick it to remove it.
3. In **Bookings** > **Add a rental**, the Add-ons list sits under The rental: tick them before you press **Check the calendar and the price**.
4. Notice is yours to judge: you may add flowers with less than 24 hours if Fleet can do it.

## After booking

1. The booking page shows the add-ons, paid or not, and any waiting for confirmation.
2. A renter asked for a chauffeur from their portal: you get a task. Press **Confirm and charge** (the card on file is charged) or **Decline**.
3. Press **Remove** and give the reason to take one off. Unpaid, it goes; paid, a refund for it waits for approval.

## Fleet: tasks and stock

Flowers and a chauffeur give Fleet a task to get them ready, due before pickup by their notice.

1. Open **Cars** > **Add-ons**. Each add-on shows its price, its notice and how many are booked in the next 30 days.
2. For seats, umbrellas and chargers, type how many we have under In stock and press **Save**. Renters cannot ask for more than are free for their dates.
3. A confirmed booking with more than we have gives you an urgent task: find another or tell the renter.

Add-on revenue is CarmaCars'' own. It is never in a commission: your commission stays on the rental charge.
', 'Add-ons', 'Add-ons in offers and rentals, confirming a chauffeur, Fleet tasks and stock.',
